  "details": "Currently, as the radius of a physbone collider is turned up, the hemispheres on the ends of the bone continue extending outward past the end of the bone. It would be convenient if there were an option to have the ends of the spheres always stay *at* the ends of the bone, i.e. to have the rounded hemispheres recede towards the MIDDLE of the bone.  This is currently already how Unity's default capsule collider works, for example.\nHere is an illustration of the current behaviour, and the alternative that I'd find convenient:",
